  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "A first name (prénom), often two or three on paper with only the first used, and the family name (nom de famille) passed down from the father, or since 2005 from either parent or both joined. Compound first names like Jean-Baptiste or Marie-Claire are common among older people. Families of Maghrebi, West African, Portuguese and Antillean heritage are part of every big French city and carry their own names alongside French ones. People say their family name first on forms and at the doctor's: 'Martin, Julie'.",
